[
  {
    "number": 116,
    "title": "Show shared session titles and projects on Pixoo",
    "body": "Sessions with shared titles now show those titles instead of ID tails when no label exists. A shared label wins, and untitled sessions keep their distinct ID tails. The owner selected layout A: a dedicated project line below the two-line identifier, retaining the activity word, child/uncertainty details and attention-only pulse. The Monitor tab shows the complete title and project.\n\nRefs #106. Source-only delivery; installed service and visible-device observations remain pending until separately requested.\n\n- Pins verified lifecycle 1.1.0, agent-state 3.3.0 and Hub 0.4.0 releases. Archive, receipt, manifest and upstream conformance checks cover the accepted bytes.\n- Uses snapshot 1.2 internally and negotiates it with the remote owner. Legacy reads keep their projections; invalid or downgraded remote replies retain stale evidence. A released-Hub loopback test verifies metadata, user-label precedence and absence of a fallback store.\n- Folds accents before bounded truncation. Synthetic examples cover titles, labels, projects, uncertainty/pulse and untitled sessions; browser canvases reproduce the exact RGB frames. See [the committed preview](https://github.com/jimmie-potts/divoom-app-upgrade/blob/7a0653589614877a7f1916d9aacf2f2ecc7f1057/docs/examples/agent-dashboard.html).\n- Preserves simulator startup, Monitor/Media selection, one writer, cadence and pagination. No hooks, personal settings, running services, live state or devices were changed. Prompt/response capture remains outside this change.\n\nValidation at `7a0653589614877a7f1916d9aacf2f2ecc7f1057`:\n\n- `npm run check`: passed; 677 tests across 75 files, plus workflow checks.\n- `npm run test:browser`: 68 passed across desktop and mobile.\n- Post-archive `npm run check:workflow` and `npm run test:workflow`: passed; 19 specifications and 10 workflow tests.\n- Focused pre-fix failures demonstrated missing metadata projection, unsupported negotiated downgrade handling, title/ID precedence and the project line; the same focused tests pass after implementation.\n- OpenSpec `gh-106-shared-titles` synchronized four capabilities and archived successfully.\n\nThe package upgrade adopts shared retention/current-status behavior. Existing fixtures now use current synthetic event timestamps; explicit unavailable-child evidence tests uncertain rollup; a retention test checks current notices survive journal pruning and stale sessions retire after 24 hours. Stream, privacy, capacity, restart and owner-cutover assertions remain covered.\n\nComparison: base and merge-base `9467f90cafe0bdf774eec2d75f66edc9e3bccaaf`; head `7a0653589614877a7f1916d9aacf2f2ecc7f1057`; `git diff 9467f90cafe0bdf774eec2d75f66edc9e3bccaaf...7a0653589614877a7f1916d9aacf2f2ecc7f1057`. Worktree clean after commit. Fresh Standards/Specification reviews, current candidate UI approval and hosted CI remain merge gates.\n",
    "state": "open",
